From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32-qspi: poll command completion and flag clear

The STM32F746 QSPI-backed SquashFS root intermittently reads corrupt data
when 64-byte indirect reads are issued back-to-back.  Serial diagnostics
between operations hide the failure, indicating that the next command can
start before the preceding transfer-complete state is fully retired.

Backport the current upstream polling model instead of relying on the old
completion interrupt race.  Also confirm that SR_TCF/SR_TEF have cleared
after writing FCR before declaring the operation complete.  This serializes
successive indirect reads at the controller's observable state transition,
without an arbitrary fixed delay.

This is a board-scoped no-SD proof-of-concept workaround.  Five consecutive
complete U-Boot-to-userspace warm boots mounted the QSPI SquashFS after the
change; the previous implementation failed intermittently.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c | 37 ++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@
 #define STM32_FIFO_TIMEOUT_US 30000
 #define STM32_BUSY_TIMEOUT_US 100000
 #define STM32_ABT_TIMEOUT_US 100000
+#define STM32_WAIT_CMD_TIMEOUT_US 5000
 #define STM32_COMP_TIMEOUT_MS 1000
 #define STM32_AUTOSUSPEND_DELAY -1
 
@@ -328,32 +329,30 @@ static int stm32_qspi_wait_nobusy(struct stm32_qspi *qspi)
 						 STM32_BUSY_TIMEOUT_US);
 }
 
-static int stm32_qspi_wait_cmd(struct stm32_qspi *qspi,
-			       const struct spi_mem_op *op)
+static int stm32_qspi_wait_cmd(struct stm32_qspi *qspi)
 {
-	u32 cr, sr;
-	int err = 0;
+	u32 sr;
+	int clear_err, err = 0;
 
-	if ((readl_relaxed(qspi->io_base + QSPI_SR) & SR_TCF) ||
-	    qspi->fmode == CCR_FMODE_APM)
+	if (qspi->fmode == CCR_FMODE_APM)
 		goto out;
 
-	reinit_completion(&qspi->data_completion);
-	cr = readl_relaxed(qspi->io_base + QSPI_CR);
-	writel_relaxed(cr | CR_TCIE | CR_TEIE, qspi->io_base + QSPI_CR);
-
-	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&qspi->data_completion,
-				msecs_to_jiffies(STM32_COMP_TIMEOUT_MS))) {
-		err = -ETIMEDOUT;
-	} else {
-		sr = readl_relaxed(qspi->io_base + QSPI_SR);
-		if (sr & SR_TEF)
-			err = -EIO;
-	}
+	err = readl_relaxed_poll_timeout_atomic(qspi->io_base + QSPI_SR, sr,
+						(sr & (SR_TEF | SR_TCF)), 1,
+						STM32_WAIT_CMD_TIMEOUT_US);
+	if (!err && (sr & SR_TEF))
+		err = -EIO;
 
 out:
 	/* clear flags */
 	writel_relaxed(FCR_CTCF | FCR_CTEF, qspi->io_base + QSPI_FCR);
+	clear_err = readl_relaxed_poll_timeout_atomic(qspi->io_base + QSPI_SR,
+							sr,
+							!(sr & (SR_TEF | SR_TCF)),
+							1,
+							STM32_WAIT_CMD_TIMEOUT_US);
+	if (!err)
+		err = clear_err;
 	if (!err)
 		err = stm32_qspi_wait_nobusy(qspi);
 
@@ -449,7 +448,7 @@ static int stm32_qspi_send(struct spi_mem *mem, const struct spi_mem_op *op)
 		goto abort;
 
 	/* wait end of tx in indirect mode */
-	err = stm32_qspi_wait_cmd(qspi, op);
+	err = stm32_qspi_wait_cmd(qspi);
 	if (err)
 		goto abort;
 
-- 
2.52.0
